Relevant tables / columns and why they matter  

Top Venues  
• mbb_games_sr.venue_name ‒ name of the building  
• mbb_games_sr.venue_capacity ‒ seats in that building (key metric)  
• mbb_games_sr.venue_city / venue_state – optional for display  

Biggest Championship Margins  
• mbb_historical_tournament_games.season ‒ must be > 2015  
• mbb_historical_tournament_games.round ‒ round = 2 → only two teams left (= National Championship)  
• mbb_historical_tournament_games.win_market / win_name / lose_market / lose_name – to build the “match‑up” text  
• mbb_historical_tournament_games.win_pts / lose_pts – point margin = win_pts ‑ lose_pts (key metric)  

Highest Scoring Games (regular or tournament, any round)  
• mbb_games_sr.season ‒ > 2010  
• mbb_games_sr.h_points  &  a_points – use (h_points + a_points) as key metric  
• mbb_games_sr.h_market / h_name / a_market / a_name – for match‑up text  
• mbb_games_sr.scheduled_date – game date to show  

Total Threes  
• mbb_games_sr.h_three_points_made & a_three_points_made – total threes for both teams (key metric)  
• Same ID / season / date / match‑up fields as above  

Typical filter conditions you will need  
1. season > 2015   (championship margin block)  
2. round = 2        (championship margin block)  
3. season > 2010    (high‑scoring + total‑threes blocks)  
4. venue_capacity IS NOT NULL AND venue_capacity > 0 (top‑venues block)  

Below are 10 exploratory BigQuery SQL snippets (LIMIT 20 each) that surface the information needed, progressing from simple column peeks to the full logic you will eventually wrap into the final UNION‑ALL answer table.

```sql
-- 1. Top 20 venues with the largest listed capacities in the play‑by‑play / box score table
SELECT DISTINCT venue_name,
       venue_capacity,
       venue_city,
       venue_state
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_games_sr`
WHERE  venue_capacity IS NOT NULL
ORDER  BY venue_capacity DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2. If you prefer team master data, peek at capacity that lives in mbb_teams
SELECT venue_name,
       venue_capacity,
       market,
       name
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_teams`
WHERE  venue_capacity IS NOT NULL
ORDER  BY venue_capacity DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Verify which values represent the National‑Championship round
SELECT DISTINCT round
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_historical_tournament_games`
WHERE  season > 2015
ORDER  BY round;
```

```sql
-- 4. Biggest winning margins in National‑Championship games since 2016
SELECT season,
       win_market || ' ' || win_name  AS winner,
       lose_market || ' ' || lose_name AS loser,
       win_pts,
       lose_pts,
       (win_pts - lose_pts)           AS margin
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_historical_tournament_games`
WHERE  season > 2015
  AND  round = 2
ORDER  BY margin DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Highest scoring D1 games since 2011 (total points by both teams)
SELECT season,
       scheduled_date,
       h_market || ' ' || h_name AS home_team,
       a_market || ' ' || a_name AS away_team,
       h_points + a_points       AS total_pts
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_games_sr`
WHERE  season > 2010
  AND  h_points IS NOT NULL AND a_points IS NOT NULL
ORDER  BY total_pts DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Alternative: using mbb_teams_games_sr (need to aggregate the two records per game)
SELECT  tg.game_id,
        ANY_VALUE(tg.season) AS season,
        MAX(tg.scheduled_date) AS scheduled_date,
        SUM(tg.points_game)    AS total_pts
FROM    `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_teams_games_sr` AS tg
WHERE   tg.season > 2010
GROUP BY tg.game_id
ORDER BY total_pts DESC
LIMIT   20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Games with the most combined three‑pointers since 2011 (using home/away fields)
SELECT season,
       scheduled_date,
       h_market || ' ' || h_name AS home_team,
       a_market || ' ' || a_name AS away_team,
       h_three_points_made + a_three_points_made AS total_threes
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_games_sr`
WHERE  season > 2010
  AND  h_three_points_made IS NOT NULL
  AND  a_three_points_made IS NOT NULL
ORDER  BY total_threes DESC
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Same total‑threes logic but via the per‑team table
SELECT  tg.game_id,
        MAX(tg.season) AS season,
        SUM(tg.three_points_made) AS total_threes
FROM    `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_teams_games_sr` AS tg
WHERE   tg.season > 2010
GROUP BY tg.game_id
ORDER BY total_threes DESC
LIMIT   20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Inspect all available box‑score columns for one extreme scoring game
SELECT *
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_games_sr`
WHERE  game_id = 'b4451a02-26c5-4005-9ac8-b06c1f71e661'  -- replace with an id from query 5
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final‑style query skeleton: union of the four blocks into one results table
-- (trimmed to 3 rows each for brevity here; expand to 5 in production)
SELECT 'Top Venues' AS Category,
       'N/A'        AS Date,
       venue_name   AS `Matchup or Venue`,
       CAST(venue_capacity AS STRING) AS `Key Metric`
FROM   (
        SELECT venue_name, venue_capacity
        FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_games_sr`
        WHERE  venue_capacity IS NOT NULL
        ORDER  BY venue_capacity DESC
        LIMIT  5
       )

UNION ALL

SELECT 'Biggest Championship Margins' AS Category,
       CAST(game_date AS STRING)      AS Date,
       win_market || ' vs ' || lose_market,
       CAST(win_pts - lose_pts AS STRING)
FROM   (
        SELECT game_date, win_market, lose_market, win_pts, lose_pts, (win_pts - lose_pts) AS margin
        FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_historical_tournament_games`
        WHERE  season > 2015 AND round = 2
        ORDER  BY margin DESC
        LIMIT  5
       )

UNION ALL

SELECT 'Highest Scoring Games',
       CAST(scheduled_date AS STRING),
       h_market || ' vs ' || a_market,
       CAST(h_points + a_points AS STRING)
FROM   (
        SELECT scheduled_date, h_market, a_market, h_points, a_points, h_points + a_points AS total_pts
        FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_games_sr`
        WHERE  season > 2010
        ORDER  BY total_pts DESC
        LIMIT  5
       )

UNION ALL

SELECT 'Total Threes',
       CAST(scheduled_date AS STRING),
       h_market || ' vs ' || a_market,
       CAST(h_three_points_made + a_three_points_made AS STRING)
FROM   (
        SELECT scheduled_date,
               h_market, a_market,
               h_three_points_made, a_three_points_made,
               h_three_points_made + a_three_points_made AS total_threes
        FROM   `bigquery-public-data.ncaa_basketball.mbb_games_sr`
        WHERE  season > 2010
        ORDER  BY total_threes DESC
        LIMIT  5
       )
LIMIT 20;
```

